        <p>Aerosol products appear simple on the surface—a press of a button and a fine spray is released. However,
            behind every stable, effective, and compliant aerosol product lies a carefully engineered chemical system.
            Aerosol chemistry governs <strong>spray performance, product stability, safety, regulatory compliance,
                coating quality, and shelf life</strong>.</p>

        <p>For students, startups, and entrepreneurs entering the aerosol industry, understanding the <strong>role of
                solvents, binders, surfactants, and additives</strong> is fundamental. This guide explains these
            building blocks using industrial formulation science, without speculation or oversimplification.</p>

        <figure style="margin:16px 0;text-align:center;">
            
            <figcaption style="font-size:0.85rem;color:#4b5563;margin-top:6px;">Internal construction of a standard
